  "conclusions": [
    "The requested two official historical-funding-rate GETs return 8891 rows per asset, source 2025-09-03 08:00 through 2026-09-09 02:00 UTC. All 3612 archive-overlap rows per asset match timestamp, absolute rate, and relative rate exactly.",
    "The API recovers 4340 of 4343 missing Jan-Jul 2026 source hours per asset, so a new sealed funding extension is feasible for those records. It still omits 2026-02-04 12:00, 2026-02-13 18:00, and 2026-05-09 06:00 UTC, as well as all seven 2025 gaps. Analytics candles exist at two of the three 2026 gaps but do not by themselves prove the hourly charge when the settlement API omits the hour.",
    "Both assets share seven missing 2025 normalized settlement hours (14 asset-hour records). Their corresponding source rows are absent in the official archived CSV bytes, including all local duplicate copies checked; no parser repair can recover them.",
    "The archived CSV ends at source 2026-02-01 00:00 UTC. Funding analytics begin at 2026-02-12 13:00 UTC. There are 276 source-hour timestamps between these sources with neither record; the metadata analytics query misses 277 hours because it includes one already-present CSV source timestamp.",
    "Analytics are OHLC funding-rate observations, not independently verified hourly payment records. There is no CSV overlap for validating a start/end or open/close mapping. The new official API fills 275 of the 276 bridge source hours, leaving February 4 at 12:00 UTC absent; analytics cannot fill that remaining bridge hour either.",
    "Absence during an exchange interruption cannot be equated to zero funding without authoritative confirmation. Existing exact-cost accounting must remain unknown if an exposed path requires an absent settlement.",
    "Funding coverage review conveys no approval to open later strategy returns or bypass the predeclared model/risk gates."
  ],
  "requiredRepairProvenance": [
    "Official historical absolute USD-per-contract hourly rates for both PF_XBTUSD and PF_ETHUSD at each missing 2025 source/settlement timestamp and all missing 2026 settlement hours, or authoritative evidence of a no-charge interval.",
    "Explicit confirmation of timestamp effective start versus settlement end, rate interval, sign convention, units, and which analytics value (if any) equals the charged historical funding rate; partial-hour applicability should also be stated.",
    "Preserve request URL and parameters, retrieval time, raw response bytes and hashes, response status/range metadata, duplicate/conflict checks, and independent exact timestamp/coverage reconciliation. Previously downloaded standalone probes without URL receipts are supporting coverage observations only.",
    "Any repaired data and parser must receive a new version and immutable manifest/protocol receipt; preserve the currently sealed data, code, and study outcomes. Do not choose funding semantics based on the resulting strategy profits."
  ]
}
